  "situation": "At the 2014 decision point, the Senate is determining the confirmation and oversight framework for the NSA Director. Historically, the Senate nominally approved directors but often exercised minimal oversight in the nomination process. The Constitution provides for presidential nomination and appointment of officers of the United States with the Senate’s advice and consent. The Senate Armed Services Committee has oversight of the Department of Defense, while the Senate Select Committee on Intelligence has a role focused on intelligence. The NSA Director also holds the United States Cyber Command commander role, bringing both organizations within the director’s responsibilities. NSA had become more publicly visible following unauthorized disclosures in 2013 and the rise of cyber intrusions.",
